# Bibliography

DeCovarT keeps **two separate citation streams**. Do not mix them.

## A. Literature (Zotero → Better BibTeX → Git)

**Source of truth** for papers / books / theses is the author's
[Zotero library](https://www.zotero.org/bastienchassagnol/library) with
**Better BibTeX (BBT)** citation keys. Do **not** invent BibTeX entries or
citekeys; add the item in Zotero first, then export.

| Path | Consumer |
|------|----------|
| `article/decovart_library.bib` | LaTeX manuscript |
| `inst/REFERENCES.bib` | Quarto vignettes (literature half) |

- Exactly these two literature copies (independent, kept in sync).
- After every Zotero export: `python3 scripts/check_bibliography.py --clean`
  (allowed fields only; DOI-dedupe; sync both copies).
- Allowed fields: `title`, `author`, `year`, `journal` **or**
  `howpublished`, `doi`, `volume`, `isbn`. Strip everything else.
- Pre-commit hook `check-bibliography` validates literature hygiene and
  `article/main.tex` citekeys (against literature **and** `packages.bib`).

GitHub issues — DOI bridge:

```markdown
- [ ] [Paper title](https://doi.org/10.xxxx/xxxxx) — `@citekey`
```

## B. Software / tools (`packages.bib` — not Zotero)

R, Bioconductor, and similar **software** citations are generated
automatically into a standalone bibliography — **not** stored in Zotero.

| Path | Consumer |
|------|----------|
| `inst/packages.bib` | Quarto vignettes (software half) |
| `article/packages.bib` | LaTeX (synced copy) |

Regenerate (from repository root):

```bash
Rscript scripts/generate_packages_bib.R
```

That script discovers packages used in **`vignettes/`** and **`article/`**
only (CRANpkg macros, `library()` / `pkg::`, plus an explicit software
allowlist for prose-only mentions such as `huge`). It does **not** dump
DESCRIPTION Imports/Suggests or the whole package dependency tree.

## C. Quarto vignette YAML (always two bibliographies)

Every `vignettes/*.qmd` must declare **both** files:

```yaml
bibliography:
  - ../inst/packages.bib
  - ../inst/REFERENCES.bib
link-citations: true
```

Example citations: literature `@wuEstimatingHeterogeneousGene2022`;
software `@R-huge`, `@R-BDgraph`, `@R-base`.

```bash
python3 scripts/check_bibliography.py --check-qmd
```

